    "narrative": "A human edited the Exit EBITDA Margin from 25.0% to 23.5%. That change flowed through to EBIT ($165 → $153), and both EBT lines dropped ($143 → $132 and $122 → $114), with taxes moving from $-36 to $-33 and from $-31 to $-28, bringing Net Income from $108 to $99 and from $92 to $85. Exit Equity fell from $1,803 to $1,679, MOIC from 3.64x to 3.39x, and IRR from 29.5% to 27.7%."
